  "query_preview": "..\nIssued at 300 AM EST Sat Nov 28 2026\n\n- Better chance for showers Sunday; mainly through the south\n\nThe upper level low that brought ran and snow continues to move\neastward, a weak negatively tilted trough will swing through the\narea today. However, it's fairly dry and the best moisture will \nbe near the points. So light rain will be possible in and around \nthe Ludington area. Another large upper level wave will deepen \nthrough the Great plains and trek through the Ohio river valley \ntomorrow. The main area of QPF continues to shift to the south but\ncan't rule out upwards of a half an inch of QPF through the south\neastern portion of the lower peninsula tomorrow. \n\n- Fair, Dry and Warming temperatures through the week\n\nWhile the before mentioned system will bring showers and a cold\nfront that will drop temperatures closer to normal, zonal flow and\nfair weather will follow through the work week. Expect \ntemperatures to rebound, upwards of 10 to 15 degrees above normal,\nwith highs back into the 50s mid to late next week. \n  \n\n- Chance for showers next weekend\n\n The guidance begins to diverge but another low could track\nthrough the region next weekend. current runs bring that low on a\nsimilar trajectory as Sunday's system, which would bring another\nchance for decent rainfall. Latest 850 temps are fairly warm so as\nof not not expecting any snow.",
